<title>FRANCE: EU HIKES WHEAT EXPORT TAXES AGAIN.</title>
<headline>EU HIKES WHEAT EXPORT TAXES AGAIN.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union raised its standing tax on soft wheat grain exports overnight to six Ecus per tonne from three Ecus, the second such increase this week, French cereals office ONIC confirmed on Thursday.</p>
<p>It also raised a tax on durum wheat to 15 Ecus per tonne from 10 Ecus and lifted other taxes on wheat and semolina.</p>
<p>There had been talk of a tax rise accompanied by a decision to accept about 400,000 tonnes of previous export bids late on Wednesday. But ONIC officials said they did not yet have any formal word from the Commission on the outcome of these bids.</p>
<p>The bids for licences then worth three Ecus in tax were presented through a daily system earlier this week and the Commission has three days to decide whether to veto each bid.  </p>
<p>A standing tax for soft wheat flour exports has risen to 8.5 Ecus from four Ecus, ONIC said.</p>
<p>The tax on durum semolina goes to 22.5 Ecus from 15.0 Ecus.</p>
<p>Officials gave the following breakdown for export taxes in Ecus per tonne.</p>
<p>    CATEGORY			(Aug 7)		 (Aug 5)</p>
<p>    Durum wheat grain	    15.00		   10.00</p>
<p>    Soft wheat grain		6.00		    3.00</p>
<p>    Durum wheat flour	    22.50		   15.00</p>
<p>    Soft wheat flour		8.50		    4.00</p>
<p>    Durum semolina		 22.50		   15.00</p>
<p>    Soft wheat semolina	   8.50		    4.00</p>
</text>
